.SP p2
.L 47.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Saspar looks like a cold servant of the Order of
.L 57.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Chaos, but underneath he simply doesn't care
.L 67.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]whether he lives; he quietly hopes to fail at his
.L 77.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]work and so be done with existence. His magic
.L 87.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]comes from strange enchanted devices rather than
.L 97.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]study: a gun that fires spells once loaded with the
.L 107.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]right bullet, and an ornate pocket watch that lets
.L 117.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]him foresee events and head off danger. He always
.L 127.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]wears a red sash over his eyes, and nobody knows
.L 137.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]whether he's truly blind.
.CP
.SH
\&Saspar: Attacks
.PP
\&Brim Shot: Calls on the spirit of Phoenix to fire a homing projectile bathed in fire.
.PP
\&Ise Shot: Calls on the spirit of Ymir to fire a frost ray that encapsulates what it hits in ice.
.PP
\&Lode Shot: Calls on the spirit of Gaia to fire a rocky blast that knocks targets off their feet.
.SH
\&Saspar: Character Hooks
.PP
\&The Order of Chaos makes Saspar and Acacia natural enemies for anyone defending the world from evil — Fukiko and Auren, whose backgrounds both feature a vague darkness to be fought, fit especially well. They can also serve as magical rivals.
